# Response headers for the landing page, in the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages
# `_headers` format.
#
# Honest limitation: GitHub Pages, which serves this directory today, does not
# read this file and does not allow custom headers. Until the site moves to a
# host (or CDN) that does, the only enforcement that actually reaches a browser
# is the equivalent `<meta>` declarations in index.html — and browsers ignore
# `frame-ancestors` and `X-Content-Type-Options` when they arrive by meta tag.
# This file exists so the intended policy is stated in one place and applies the
# moment a header-capable host serves it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com
